0px;"><div class=3D"fbb737a4"><div class=3D"ds-collapsible-text" style=3D""=
><div><span>Meridian is a personal, single-user markets and investing appli=
cation that I'm designing/creating. For example, it could have a portfolio =
page, a news page, and more pages (maybe 4-5 more), and many sub-pages. Als=
o, as a secondary layer on top, these areas could potentially be able to re=
ference and enrich each other where relevant =E2=80=94 e.g. a news story co=
uld be checked against a portfolio's holdings.

I want you to create a really nice UI design - that works - for the Portfol=
io page and its sub-pages. You may add things if you deem it beneficial.

The portfolio page will have these subpages:
- Overview
- Holdings
- Performance
- Analysis

Think hard about the right architecture and structure for it, from scratch.=
 Take your time and think really hard about this.

Indispensable content for a portfolio feature =E2=80=94 no imposed structur=
e:

Total portfolio value, a holdings table, a performance chart,=20
Cash balance
List of individual holdings (quantity, price, value, P&amp;L per holding)
Value over time (a performance chart)

I want you to think hard. You can do what you want. Adhere to your best vis=
ion, regarding pages, sub-pages, content, metrics, visuals, etc. One rule o=
f thumb is that visual things are generally preferred over long text, as it=
's quicker to scan.

In terms of content, data, etc., you can add whatever you want. The list ab=
ove is just things that should be there (but those are in all versions rega=
rdless). In terms of content, what you end up adding will for the vast majo=
rity not be in that list.

I want something that is cool to look at. Not something that is boring and =
basic. Make it stand out somehow.</span></div></div><div class=3D"ds-collap=
